From 5958e4c92fdca04da94d0871ec06a4d5c9571414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:43:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 52/53] civ45: luxury and food resources inside the borders
 lift every city

Issue 276 (notes/freeciv45/design/resources.md). Each kind of luxury
resource (Gold, Gems, Silk, Wine, Spice, Furs, Ivory, Whales) inside a
civ's borders makes one citizen content in every city; each kind of
food resource (Wheat, Buffalo, Fruit, Pheasant, Game, Fish, Oasis)
raises every city's size cap by one and its health by 5%. Copies of a
kind count once.

Lua recomputes the kinds held from the map each turn and keeps a hidden
"<Resource> Supply" small wonder per kind in the capital, so the effects
are native and the AI weighs them. Gains and losses are told once.
---
